---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Example from '../../components/Example.astro';
import palettes from '../../../../tokens/palettes.json';
const names=Object.keys(palettes);
const title=name=>name[0].toUpperCase()+name.slice(1);
const sections=[{id:'activate',title:'Page defaults'},{id:'roles',title:'Semantic roles'},...names.map(name=>({id:name,title:title(name)})),{id:'overrides',title:'Overrides'},{id:'glass',title:'Glass material'}];
const demo=name=>'<div class="grid" data-palette="'+name+'">\n'+['light','dark'].map(mode=>`  <section data-theme="${mode}">\n    <article class="card stack">\n      <h3>${title(name)} / ${mode}</h3>\n      <p>Page colours, surfaces, borders, links and actions share this palette.</p>\n      <p><a href="#activate">Explore the palette</a> · <span class="badge">New</span></p>\n      <div class="row">\n        <button type="button">Primary action</button>\n        <button type="button" class="secondary">Secondary</button>\n      </div>\n      <div><label for="${name}-${mode}-name">Project name</label><input id="${name}-${mode}-name" placeholder="My project"></div>\n      <p><span class="badge" data-variant="success" data-appearance="solid">Success</span> <span class="badge" data-variant="danger" data-appearance="solid">Error</span></p>\n    </article>\n  </section>`).join('\n')+'\n</div>';
---
<DocsLayout title="Colour palettes" active="palettes" sections={sections}>
<p class="doc-kicker">THEMES / PALETTES</p><h1>Eight coordinated palettes</h1>
<p class="doc-lead">Default is the standard palette: white and black foundations with Blue Teal actions, links and main headings. Choose Mono, Sand, Ocean, Cobalt, Citrus, Violet or Forest once on a parent. Ordinary HTML and existing component hooks inherit the colours.</p>
<Example id="activate" title="Choose the whole site's palette" description="data-theme controls light, dark or system mode. data-palette controls the colour family. Both are independent of material, shape and other shared settings." render={false} html={'<html lang="en" data-theme="auto" data-palette="ocean">\n  <!-- Load reva.css; your ordinary HTML inherits the colours. -->\n</html>'}/>
<p>Omitting data-palette uses Default. Mono remains available for monochrome primary actions and links. Primary fills are #1F6E8C in light mode and #2E8A99 in dark mode; dark links use #65BBC7 for contrast. For scoped styling, choose the palette on the .reva boundary. Changing data-theme inside a palette changes the mode without resetting its colour family. Semantic success, warning and error colours retain their meanings, including in Mono.</p>
<Example id="roles" title="The default action palette" description="Exact solid role fills, with foregrounds adapted to each mode. Secondary uses the existing class; semantic roles use the shared variant attribute." html={'<div class="grid" data-palette="default" data-fill="solid">\n'+['light','dark'].map(mode=>`  <section data-theme="${mode}" class="card stack">\n    <h3>${mode} actions</h3>\n    <div class="row">\n      <button type="button">Primary</button>\n      <button type="button" class="secondary">Secondary</button>\n      <button type="button" data-variant="success">Success</button>\n      <button type="button" data-variant="warning">Warning</button>\n      <button type="button" data-variant="danger">Danger</button>\n    </div>\n  </section>`).join('\n')+'\n</div>'}/>
{names.map(name=><Example id={name} title={title(name)+(name==='default'?' — standard':'')} description="The same markup in light and dark mode. No palette attributes are repeated on the components." html={demo(name)}/>)}
<Example id="overrides" title="Local palettes and explicit overrides" description="A local palette installs a complete coordinated set. On the same element, explicit data-accent and data-tone override its primary and surface colours respectively. A nearer palette resets inherited colour overrides; unrelated settings continue inheriting." html={'<section class="stack" data-palette="ocean">\n  <button type="button">Inherited Ocean</button>\n  <article class="card" data-palette="mono">\n    <h3>Local Mono</h3>\n    <button type="button">Mono action</button>\n  </article>\n  <article class="card" data-palette="forest" data-accent="violet" data-tone="warm">\n    <h3>Forest with warm surfaces</h3>\n    <p><a href="#activate">Links keep the Forest colour.</a></p>\n    <button type="button">Explicit violet action</button>\n  </article>\n</section>'}/>
<Example id="glass" title="Use the same palette with glass" description="Load reva.glass.css after the core. Palette tokens feed the material; glass links use the palette's text foreground for stronger readability. Styled text inputs retain their normal backing." glass html={'<section data-palette="ocean" data-theme="dark" data-material="glass">\n  <article class="card">\n    <h3>Ocean glass</h3>\n    <p>The material uses the parent palette surfaces.</p>\n    <button type="button">Primary action</button>\n  </article>\n</section>'}/>
</DocsLayout>
